  "final": "Done. The cause was `reorder_qty` in `inventory/stock.py`. It used floor division (`need // pack_size`), so it ordered fewer units than needed. The 183 failures were mostly one test's subtests, each printing a block of output.\n\nI changed the line to ceiling division: `packs = -(-need // pack_size)`. `python3 -m unittest` now exits 0 with all 7 tests OK. I didn't add a regression test because `test_reorder_rounds_up_to_whole_pack` already covers this.",
